Architecture

    Compare and contrast the types of frontend development you used in your full stack project, including Express HTML, JavaScript, and the single-page application (SPA).
        Express HTML was used to build and format the layout of the pages within the website. Javascript was then used to allow the user to interact and move around the different pages. SPA provides a very different user experience than the other website as all the elements exist within one page which allows for the website to be more efficient and feel more seamless.
    Why did the backend use a NoSQL MongoDB database?
        One of the reasons that NoSQL MongoDB was used is that the file type is similar to that of Javascripts JSON this makes for an ease of transfer. 

Functionality

    How is JSON different from Javascript and how does JSON tie together the frontend and backend development pieces?
        JSON is an important piece of the puzzle as it interacts with Javascript and allows us to tie the front end of Javascript to the database within Mongo.
    Provide instances in the full stack process when you refactored code to improve functionality and efficiencies, and name the benefits that come from reusable user interface (UI) components.
        The benefits of creating and having reusable user interface components is that it allows for you to save money and time in terms of development. This also lowers code complexity which means that updating it in the future can be easier as instead of having to update individual components you only have to update one.

